issue_context.body:
If an assembly is marked with `PrimaryInteropAssemblyAttribute`, all public value types are validated for TypeEquivalence. This works without issue unless the value type contains a method, at which point a failure will occur:

```
  System.TypeLoadException: Could not load the structure '<TYPE_NAME>' from assembly '<ASSEMBLY_NAME>'. The structure is marked as eligible for type equivalence, but it has a method.
```

However, if the type only has methods that are marked `static`, this should be permitted.


Fails as expected:
```csharp
struct T
{
    public int F;
    public void M() { }
}
```

Consider supported:
```csharp
struct T
{
    public int F;
    public static void M() { }
}
```

comments:
Failing repro code:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Runtime.InteropServices;

[assembly:PrimaryInteropAssembly(1,0)]

public struct T
{
    public int F;
    public static void M() { }
}

public class Program
{
    public static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine(typeof(T).Name);
    }
}
```

review_comments:
I think we should also have a regression based test. Let's attempt to load a type that will throw and validate the exception type is expected. Create a new type called `ValueTypeWithMethod` and use that to verify it throws as expected. We can use a local static function like below, which can be pasted within this method. Remember to update the name of `TestLoadingValueTypeWithStaticMethod`.

```csharp
Assert.Throws<TypeLoadException>(() => LoadInvalidType());

[MethodImpl (MethodImplOptions.NoInlining)]
static void LoadInvalidType()
{
        Console.WriteLine($"-- {typeof(ValueTypeWithMethod).Name}");
}
```
